Quick update: I checked the browser console when runnning the web variant as a container. When i hit the button "Create git repository", i see internal errors with the following message:

`{
    "name": "UnknownError",
    "data": {
        "message": "Error: Git is not installed\n    at initGit (src/project/project.ts:352:34)\n    at <anonymous> (src/server/routes/project.ts:76:36)\n    at dispatch (../../node_modules/.bun/hono@4.10.7/node_modules/hono/dist/compose.js:22:23)\n    at <anonymous> (../../node_modules/.bun/hono-openapi@1.1.2+e879d1208fed8dbe/node_modules/hono-openapi/dist/index.js:461:11)\n    at dispatch (../../node_modules/.bun/hono@4.10.7/node_modules/hono/dist/compose.js:22:23)\n    at <anonymous> (../../node_modules/.bun/hono@4.10.7/node_modules/hono/dist/validator/validator.js:81:18)\n    at processTicksAndRejections (native:7:39)"
    }
}`

So i think this could be a bug when running opencode as a container image.

@kesor @tgwfc1012-cyber just to be clear, have either of you had this issue after March 8th?

> A plausible cause might be the added delay/latency.

Is that plausible? how/why would that matter?
